content.text:
The awakening modal test fails because the modal text may not include "MINOR BREAKTHROUGH" (the eyebrow does, not modalText) or "Qi Condensation I" maybe in title, not text. Let's inspect. The modal eyebrow is "SPIRIT MINOR BREAKTHROUGH", and the title is "Mortal → Qi Condensation I". `modalText` doesn't include those. The test checks `#modalText`, so adjust to check `#modalEyebrow` and `#modalTitle`. Fix test.

But also, this reveals a UX detail: the modal body for Mortal says "Gather your breath and refine the spirit. A minor breakthrough carries you one stage deeper." which is fine. The title shows the transition. Good.

Update test:
```js
const eyebrow = await page.locator('#modalEyebrow').textContent();
const title = await page.locator('#modalTitle').textContent();
check('...', eyebrow.includes('MINOR BREAKTHROUGH') && title.includes('Qi Condensation I'));
```
Run again.

